# One direct external dependency per line: <crate-name> <reason it is allowed>.
# Transitive crates are not listed here; deny.toml gates them by licenses, bans, sources, advisories.
# Only crates under crates/edge/ and xtask may depend on the crates listed here.
ra-ap-rustc_lexer the lexer of rustc itself, so xtask reads Rust source exactly as the compiler does
serde_json reads the cargo metadata output in xtask
serde the derive backend every edge config struct deserializes with
toml the config file format: it keeps a value tree, so environment overrides merge before deserialization
tokio the multi-thread executor behind the serving runtime, its timers and its signals
hyper the HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 server implementation edge/http drives
hyper-util the auto protocol-selection server connection and tokio glue for hyper
http the shared request/response value types hyper speaks
http-body the body trait hyper sends and receives over
http-body-util body combinators that turn a kernel Chunks stream into a hyper body
bytes the buffer type hyper's bodies carry
form_urlencoded decodes application/x-www-form-urlencoded POST bodies into query pairs
percent-encoding decodes percent-escapes in request paths
rusqlite SQLite bindings with the bundled C sources: the only store edge/sqlite speaks
